1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:02,413
Why does learning to trade take so long?

2
00:00:02,955 --> 00:00:09,543
Partly because the market gives you so few chances to practise. Earnings, for example, come four times a year.

3
00:00:10,043 --> 00:00:16,849
A trend can take weeks to play out. Earnings come four times a year, and central banks meet about eight times a year.

4
00:00:17,197 --> 00:00:21,197
It can take years to see each kind of event more than a handful of times.

5
00:00:21,697 --> 00:00:25,140
On Meme Street, a full trading day takes thirty real minutes.

6
00:00:25,549 --> 00:00:32,874
There are earnings every couple of days, economic data with forecasts, and a two minute Daily Chart to practise on, every day.

7
00:00:33,374 --> 00:00:36,675
Get a week of practice in an evening, at memestreet.net.

